## NAME
vtium-config - set up the fonts and settings of vtium, a terminal for the Linux console

## SYNOPSIS
@SYNOPSIS@

## DESCRIPTION
@DESCRIPTION@

vtium reads `/etc/vtium/vtium.conf` only when it starts on a VT, so a change that install makes takes effect when vtium starts again. install offers to restart vtium on the VTs it runs on. See vtium.conf(5) for the file and its settings.

`vtium config`, a command of the console, runs vtium-config with the words that follow it.

## COMMANDS
@COMMANDS@

## OPTIONS
The options come before the command. Run as root, vtium-config refuses each option that names a path or a program, so that it reads and writes only `/etc/vtium` and its font set directory, and runs only the programs it was built with.

@OPTIONS@

## EXIT STATUS
@EXIT STATUS@

## ENVIRONMENT
= `VISUAL`, `EDITOR`
The editor that edit opens, `VISUAL` first. Without either, edit opens vi.

= `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`
The directory that holds `vtium/drafts`, `vtium/library.conf` and `vtium/vtium-config.conf`, `~/.config` when unset.

## FILES
= `~/.config/vtium/drafts/NAME.conf`
The drafts: your working copies of vtium.conf.

= `~/.config/vtium/library.conf`
The looks, heads and rules that the library keeps outside any draft.

= `~/.config/vtium/vtium-config.conf`
vtium-config's own settings, such as how many earlier vtium.conf files history keeps.

= `/etc/vtium/vtium.conf`
The file that install writes.

= `/etc/vtium/fonts`
The font sets, each in a file `NAME.vtfrit`.

## SEE ALSO
vtium(8), vtium.conf(5)
